--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/coding-agent/docs/rpc-strict-start.md
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# Deferred strict rpc-ui startup (isolated Linux prototype)
+
+Launch the normal interactive mode with `--mode rpc-ui --strict-start`. The first ready frame exposes
+`strictStartup: strict-start-v1`, the effective explicit-answer interaction policy, and strict startup
+platform/ownership/native-format/budget constraints. No ordinary Session/extensions/UI exist yet.
+Negotiate protocol v2, then send one explicit `strict_start` with `intent: continue`, an opaque catalog
+reference and authorized canonical `expectedCwd`; or `intent: new` without a reference. Repeated starts
+are refused. `get_strict_state` is readonly and never replays; `cancel_strict_start` preserves known
+cancelled/cancelling/unknown outcomes. An open result binds native Session ID and current catalog identity.
+
+Continue owns the native exclusive lease and pins source/parent/Session/cwd identities before ordinary
+runtime initialization. Unknown lease acquisition fails. Native persistence never retargets to a sibling,
+repairs/retries an uncertain operation automatically, truncates the Session body, or displaces a replacement.
+
+Whole rewrites retain the carrier inode. Exclusive immutable native JSONL generations and bounded authenticated
+metadata are prepared in `.<basename>.omp-generations`, an fd-bound `user.omp-generation-v1` xattr announces
+current/previous commit offsets, only the seven-byte header discriminator changes from `session` to `ompgen1`,
+and a checksummed commit is appended. Native readers resolve the winning generation plus carrier append suffix.
+Incomplete final commit retains old logical state and refuses further writes. Partial conversion is incompatible;
+complete committed missing/corrupt controls are errors. Prepared data remains for native-only investigation.
+This is software process-crash persistence, without fsync/power-loss or hostile same-UID guarantees.
+
+Budgets: logical body128MiB, carrier256MiB, retained generations512MiB/64 generations/128 entries;
+head/metadata/marker1KiB each. Catalog reads carrier prefix16KiB + bounded controls6144 bytes + winning
+prefix16KiB, authenticating prefix bytes without hashing history. Full loaders verify full body hashes.
+Unsupported platform/xattrs and budget limits fail closed; no unsafe GC fallback exists.
+
+Matched TUI/CLI continue reads/writes the logical native data. Explicit native New/fork/branch uses a fresh owned
+backend and genuine logical serialization; it is not conflict recovery. Generation-v1 generic delete/move/GC/
+strip/compress is explicitly unsupported or skipped. Hardlink aliases without controls are partial errors;
+multi-link full publication refuses. A raw carrier copy/restore is not a backup: even losing xattr AND sidecars
+retains `ompgen1`, making baseline TUI refuse stale history. Use native flattened pack/render export under ownership.
+Rollback requires a verified flattened export and exclusive access, not an older binary over extended data.
+
+Nested extended artifact Sessions are logically flattened for explicit native copy/fork/branch-copy operations. Real child leases and complete shared-reader cuts are prepared before destination publication; occupied/unknown/corrupt/budget cases refuse. Fresh files use Linux O_TMPFILE plus fd-bound linkat with no-clobber names; there is no rename/unlink/truncate fallback. Copy is bounded to8192 entries/256 directories/32 levels/64 native children/128MiB total body. Generic archive pack of nested extended artifacts currently refuses; parent-only flattened pack is supported. Native branch without copyArtifacts retains its ordinary no-copy semantics.
